{
  "name": "topo_pen_surface_raycast",
  "description": "Topology Pen P0 (doc/topopen_p0_plan.md): the CONS stage's background-surface raycast branch, probed through GET /api/surface-raycast. Every case's camera uses the 'focus-point trick' -- the viewport CENTRE pixel's ray passes through the camera's `focus` point EXACTLY (a property of the lookAt-based camera construction, independent of azimuth/elevation/distance) -- so a case sets `focus` to the exact world point it wants the raycast to land on. All expected numbers are hand-derived analytically (fan-triangle cross products, point-to-segment distances) and cross-checked with an independent Python re-implementation of screenRay/lookAt/sphericalToCartesian; no reference 3D modeling tool was used (P0 is pinned-geometry only per the task brief).",
  "provenance": {
    "schema": 1,
    "source": "analytic",
    "reference": "analytic",
    "method": "hand + independent Python re-derivation",
    "captured_utc": "unknown",
    "harness": null,
    "task": "topopen-p0",
    "notes": "Hand-authored fixture for the topology-pen P0 background-surface-raycast plumbing (doc/topopen_p0_plan.md). Every hit point/normal/nearestVert/nearestEdge is derived analytically from the loaded mesh's own vertex coordinates (fan-triangle normals, point-to-segment closest-point) and the camera's guaranteed centre-pixel-through-focus property; cross-checked against a standalone Python replica of math.d's screenRay/lookAt/sphericalToCartesian (not committed) to bound the sub-pixel sampling error at <=0.016 world units for every case, comfortably inside the suite's 0.02 tolerance. 'bg_cube_bottom_face' stands in for the plan's 'bg_sphere_center' case -- hand-authoring an exact UV-sphere fixture (face indices + tangent-plane normals) was not practical without generator tooling; a third distinct cube face (-Y, previously untested by the top/+X/-X cases) exercises the same normal-direction diversity goal. 'bg_quad_tilted_normal' (review NIT-4) is 'bg_quad_offcenter' rotated 30deg about world X -- every other case's background face is axis-aligned, so this is the only case whose expected normal has all three components nonzero, exercising pickSurfaceRay's cross(b-a,c-a) fan-triangle normal against a genuinely oblique FACE (not just an oblique camera ray)."
  },
  "tolerance": 0.02,
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "bg_cube_topface_center",
      "input": [
        { "reset": true },
        { "endpoint": "command", "argstring": "tool.pipe.attr constrain enabled true" },
        { "endpoint": "command", "argstring": "tool.pipe.attr constrain geometry point" },
        { "endpoint": "command", "argstring": "layer.add name:Bg" },
        { "endpoint": "load-mesh", "body": {
            "vertices": [[-0.5,-0.5,-0.5],[0.5,-0.5,-0.5],[0.5,0.5,-0.5],[-0.5,0.5,-0.5],
                         [-0.5,-0.5,0.5],[0.5,-0.5,0.5],[0.5,0.5,0.5],[-0.5,0.5,0.5]],
            "faces": [[0,3,2,1],[4,5,6,7],[0,4,7,3],[1,2,6,5],[3,7,6,2],[0,1,5,4]]
          } },
        { "endpoint": "command", "argstring": "layer.setVisible index:1 value:true" },
        { "endpoint": "command", "argstring": "layer.select index:0" },
        { "endpoint": "camera", "body": {
            "azimuth": 0.4, "elevation": 0.6, "distance": 4,
            "focus": {"x": 0, "y": 0.5, "z": 0}
          } }
      ],
      "raycast": { "x": 475, "y": 300 },
      "expected": {
        "hit": true, "layer": 1, "face": 4,
        "point": [0, 0.5, 0], "normal": [0, 1, 0]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "bg_quad_offcenter",
      "input": [
        { "reset": true },
        { "endpoint": "command", "argstring": "tool.pipe.attr constrain enabled true" },
        { "endpoint": "command", "argstring": "tool.pipe.attr constrain geometry point" },
        { "endpoint": "command", "argstring": "layer.add name:Bg" },
        { "endpoint": "load-mesh", "body": {
            "vertices": [[-10,0,-10],[10,0,-10],[10,0,10],[-10,0,10]],
            "faces": [[0,2,1],[0,3,2]]
          } },
        { "endpoint": "command", "argstring": "layer.setVisible index:1 value:true" },
        { "endpoint": "command", "argstring": "layer.select index:0" },
        { "endpoint": "camera", "body": {
            "azimuth": 0.35, "elevation": 0.87, "distance": 6,
            "focus": {"x": 3, "y": 0, "z": -2}
          } }
      ],
      "raycast": { "x": 475, "y": 300 },
      "expected": {
        "hit": true, "layer": 1, "face": 0,
        "point": [3, 0, -2], "normal": [0, 1, 0],
        "nearestVert": [10, 0, -10],
        "nearestEdge": [[-10, 0, -10], [10, 0, 10]]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "bg_quad_tilted_normal",
      "_comment": "NIT-3-P0-review NIT-4: every other case hits an axis-aligned face, so pickSurfaceRay's interpolated normal (cross(b-a,c-a) from the hit face's own verts) is exercised only by ray DIRECTION, never by a genuinely oblique FACE normal -- a sign/winding bug there would still pass every other case. This is 'bg_quad_offcenter' rotated 30 degrees about the world X axis (R_x(30deg) applied to every vertex, the expected point, and the expected normal), so every expected number here is derivable by applying the SAME rotation matrix to that already-verified case's numbers rather than a fresh independent derivation: R_x(30): y'=y*cos(t)-z*sin(t), z'=y*sin(t)+z*cos(t), t=pi/6, sin(t)=0.5, cos(t)=0.8660254 (sqrt(3)/2). The resulting normal (0, 0.8660254, 0.5) has no zero-or-one axis components at all -- not aligned with X, Y, or Z.",
      "input": [
        { "reset": true },
        { "endpoint": "command", "argstring": "tool.pipe.attr constrain enabled true" },
        { "endpoint": "command", "argstring": "tool.pipe.attr constrain geometry point" },
        { "endpoint": "command", "argstring": "layer.add name:Bg" },
        { "endpoint": "load-mesh", "body": {
            "vertices": [[-10,5,-8.660254],[10,5,-8.660254],[10,-5,8.660254],[-10,-5,8.660254]],
            "faces": [[0,2,1],[0,3,2]]
          } },
        { "endpoint": "command", "argstring": "layer.setVisible index:1 value:true" },
        { "endpoint": "command", "argstring": "layer.select index:0" },
        { "endpoint": "camera", "body": {
            "azimuth": 0.5, "elevation": 0.5, "distance": 6,
            "focus": {"x": 3, "y": 1.0, "z": -1.7320508}
          } }
      ],
      "raycast": { "x": 475, "y": 300 },
      "expected": {
        "hit": true, "layer": 1, "face": 0,
        "point": [3, 1.0, -1.7320508], "normal": [0, 0.8660254, 0.5],
        "nearestVert": [10, 5, -8.660254],
        "nearestEdge": [[-10, 5, -8.660254], [10, -5, 8.660254]]
      }
    },
